<div class="card">
  <div class="cardHd">Privacy</div>
  <div class="cardBd">

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>1) Discord account information</strong><br>
      We store your Discord user ID, username, display name, and avatar so you can
      sign in and have a PlayCtrl.me profile. This information is kept with your
      account and is refreshed when you sign in. Your display name and avatar may
      be visible on your control page, in groups, on leaderboards, and in Discover
      if you choose to appear there.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>2) Profile, device, and community settings</strong><br>
      We store your control page settings, command permissions, paired device
      records, whitelist, favorites, group memberships, and profile customization
      so those features continue to work. They are kept until you change them,
      remove them, or the related account or group is removed. Public control page
      information is visible to anyone who can open the link. Private settings and
      device credentials are not shown publicly.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>3) Files uploaded for commands</strong><br>
      Files uploaded through PlayCtrl.me are normally stored for up to <strong>24 hours</strong>
      so they can be delivered and reused from your recent uploads. A file may be
      kept longer while a command is queued or when it must be preserved with a
      safety report. Anyone with its direct file link may be able to view it while
      it exists.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>4) Screenshots and webcam responses</strong><br>
      Screenshot and webcam response files are normally stored for up to
      <strong>6 hours</strong>. They are stored so the requested result can be returned
      to the authorized user.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>5) Commands sent while someone is away</strong><br>
      If away mode queuing is enabled, command details are stored until delivered
      or until the <strong>24 hour away window</strong> ends.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>6) Command history and activity records</strong><br>
      PlayCtrl.me records command activity, including the users involved, command
      type, time, and command details needed for history, moderation, rate limits,
      and abuse prevention. The receiving user can see their latest
      <strong>15 commands</strong>. The underlying activity records currently have no
      automatic expiration and may also include an IP address and browser or client
      information. Those internal details are limited to site administration and
      moderation use.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>7) Message boards</strong><br>
      A personal control page message board keeps its latest
      <strong>100 messages</strong>. A group message board keeps its latest
      <strong>50 messages</strong>. Messages are visible to people who can view the
      related control page or group. Older messages are removed as new ones are
      posted.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>8) Reports and moderation information</strong><br>
      Reports, strikes, bans, report details, and media saved as report evidence
      currently have no automatic expiration. They are kept for safety, moderation,
      appeals, and preventing repeat abuse. Report information and preserved media
      are visible to site administrators and moderators, with limited related
      information shown to the affected user where appropriate.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>9) Login sessions and cookies</strong><br>
      PlayCtrl.me uses a secure login cookie to keep you signed in. The cookie lasts
      for up to <strong>15 days</strong>. Logging out removes the active server side
      session. A short lived OAuth cookie is also used while completing Discord
      sign in.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>10) What other people can see</strong><br>
      Your control page is shareable by design. If Discover is enabled, guests and
      members can see your listed profile and presence. Command totals may appear
      on public leaderboards unless you disable leaderboard visibility in your
      profile settings. Information posted to a group is visible according to that
      group's access settings.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>11) Deletion requests</strong><br>
      Some information can be changed or removed directly from your profile. For
      account information or records that cannot be removed there, contact a site
      administrator through the PlayCtrl.me community Discord. Security, moderation,
      or legal records may still need to be retained.
    </p>

    <p class="muted">
      <strong>Last updated: June 23, 2026.</strong>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
